Vol. 1 No. 3, 17 Sept 1949. Biographical note: the game score in the Chess
Bulletin shows the Australian player's name as 'D. R. Armstrong' but The Times
(29 Aug 1949, p7) has 'D. M. Armstrong' which is much more likely. David Malet
Armstrong (1926-2014), an Australian philosopher (see Wikipedia), played for
Oxford University in the 1953 and 1954 Varsity chess matches. He would have
been studying at the University of Sydney in 1949.} 0-1

